1)	An automated roller compactor repairing device, comprising:

i)	a platform 101  associated with said device to accommodate a roller compactor, configured with multiple motorized wheels 102 to maneuver said platform 101  over a ground surface, wherein a laser-based sensor is installed over said platform 101  to determine level of said surface and sends acquired data to a microcontroller link  115 ed with said laser-based sensor that in turn activates a telescopically operated rod 103 attached in between each of said wheels 102 and platform 101  to stabilize said platform 101  over said surface;
ii)	an artificial intelligence-based imaging unit  104 mounted over said platform 101  to capture multiple images of surroundings for detecting dimension of said compactor present in proximity to said platform 101, wherein said imaging unit  104 transmits acquired data to said microcontroller that activate a pair of L-shaped pneumatic bar 105 attached over said platform 101  to extend/retract for clasping main frame of said compactor in a secured manner via a pair of motorized clamps  106  attached with said bars as an end effector;
iii)	a LiDAR (Light Detection and Ranging) configured on said platform 101  and synced with said imaging unit  104 to detect presence and exact location of rivets over said compactor, wherein plurality of robotic arms 107 are arranged on said platform 101, each integrated with a motorized chuck  108 , and said chuck  108  is installed with a facing tool 109 that is positioned over lateral sides of vibrating wheels 102 of said compactor, and said microcontroller simultaneously actuates said chuck  108  to rotate for translating said tool on said rivets in view of disengaging said vibrating wheels 102 from said compactor;
iv)	a speaker 110 mounted on said platform 101 that is activated by said microcontroller for notifying said user to manually position new vibrating wheels 102 over said compactor, followed by actuation of multiple robotic grippers 111 installed on said platform 101 to securely grip said positioned vibrating wheels 102 in contact with said compactor, and synchronously said microcontroller actuates said facing tool 109 for engaging said vibrating wheels 102 with said compactor; 
v)	a dust sensor positioned on said platform 101 that works in synchronization with said imaging unit 104 for detecting level of said dust over said compactor, wherein an electronic nozzle 112 is attached with a chamber 113 stored with a cleaning solution and configured at said platform 101 that is activated by said microcontroller for continuously dispensing said cleaning solution on said compactor;
vi)	a motorized disc 114 installed with said platform 101 via an inverted L-shaped telescopically operated link 115 and equipped with plurality of bristles 116, wherein said microcontroller actuates said link 115 to extend, followed by actuation of said disc 114 to rotate for scrubbing said compactor via said bristles 116;
vii)	an electronic valve 117 attached with a vessel 118 stored with water and configured at said platform 101, wherein upon scrubbing of said entire compactor with cleaning solution, as processed by said microcontroller upon detection via said imaging unit, said microcontroller actuates said valve 117 for dispensing said water on said compactor in synchronization with actuation of said disc 114 for scrubbing said compactor to rinse said compactor with water; and
viii)	a corrosion detection sensor integrated on said platform 101 for detecting presence of rust on said compactor, wherein a container 120 stored with an anti-rust solution is arranged on said platform 101 and integrated with an electronically controlled spout 119 that is actuated by said microcontroller to spray said solution onto said compactor in order to remove said detected rust, only in case said rust is detected on said compactor.

