3)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein an inverted U-shaped handle 122 is configured with said platform 101 for allowing said user to maneuver said platform 101 from one place to another as per preferences.

4)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a level sensor is embedded within said chamber 113 and vessel 118 for detecting level of said cleaning solution and water, respectively, and as soon as said detected level recedes a threshold level, said microcontroller sends an alert on said computing unit for notifying said user to re-fill said chamber 113 and vessel 118.

5)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein said microcontroller is wirelessly link 115 ed with said computing unit via a communication module which includes, but not limited to Wi-Fi (Wireless Fidelity) module, Bluetooth module, GSM (Global System for Mobile Communication) module.

6)	The device as claimed in claim 1, wherein a battery is associated with said device for powering up electrical and electronically operated components associated with said device.

1.	A DNA construct for providing cold induced sweetening (CIS) resistance in host plant, said DNA construct comprises: one or more gene fragments encoding siRNA; at least one promotor; and at least one transcriptional terminator,
wherein the gene fragments are selected from SEQ ID NO: 1 and SEQ ID NO: 2. 

2.	The DNA construct as claimed in claim 1, wherein the gene fragment of SEQ ID NO: 1 encodes siRNA targeting UDP-glucose pyrophosphorylase (UGPase); and the gene fragment of SEQ ID NO: 2 encodes siRNA targeting vacoular acid invertase (VaInv) enzyme.

3.	The DNA construct as claimed in claim 1, wherein the construct further comprises: a spacer-GBSS intron of SEQ ID NO: 3; and wherein the construct is a hairpin RNA (hpRNA) construct encoding the siRNA capable of down-regulating target gene selected from StUGPase and StVaInv by RNAi mediated gene silencing.

4.	The DNA construct as claimed in claim 1, wherein the construct is cloned in a vector with flanking restriction endonuclease sites including but not limited to BamHI, XbaI and SacI.

5.	The DNA construct as claimed in claim 1, wherein the promotor is selected from Cauliflower mosaic virus (CaMV) 35S (CaMV35S) promotor; and wherein the transcriptional terminator including but not limited to NOS-T.

6.	The DNA construct as claimed in claim 1, wherein the host plant is Solanum tuberosum. 

7.	A binary vector comprising: a) a vector backbone of pBI121; and b) DNA construct as defined in claim 1.

8.	A method of preparing the DNA construct as claimed in claim 1, said method comprising the steps of:
(a)	identifying and isolating gene fragments selected from SEQ ID NO: 1 and 2 from total genomic DNA of host plant;
(b)	cloning the gene fragments of SEQ ID NO: 1, 2 and GBSS intron of SEQ ID NO: 3 in a pUC19 vector with flanking suitable restriction endonuclease sites to obtain a template plasmid pUC19::CISCOM-S-In;
(c)	amplifying the template to obtain an antisense fragment;
(d)	ligating the antisense fragment into pUC19::CISCOM-S-In to get the DNA construct pUC::CISCOM-S-In-As, and
(e)	preparing a binary vector cassette pBI121::CISCOM by subcloning the DNA construct onto pBI121 binary vector backbone.

9.	The method as claimed in claim 8, wherein the template plasmid is amplified using primer pair of SEQ ID NO: 4-17.

10.	A method for inducing cold induced sweetening (CIS) resistance in host plant, said method comprising the steps of:
(a)	identifying and isolating gene fragments selected from SEQ ID NO: 1 and 2 from total genomic DNA of host plant;
(b)	cloning the gene fragments of SEQ ID NO: 1, 2 and GBSS intron of SEQ ID NO: 3 in pUC19 vector with flanking suitable restriction endonuclease sites to obtain template plasmid pUC19::CISCOM-S-In;
(c)	amplifying the template using primer pair of SEQ ID NO: 4-17 to obtain an antisense fragment;
(d)	ligating the antisense fragment into pUC19::CISCOM-S-In to get the DNA construct pUC::CISCOM-S-In-As;
(e)	preparing a binary vector cassette pBI121::CISCOM by subcloning the DNA construct onto pBI121 binary vector backbone;
(f)	mobilizing said binary vector cassette into Agrobacterium sp. to obtain transformed Agrobacterium, and
(g)	mediating transformation of the host plant using the transformed Agrobacterium,
wherein the host plant is Solanum tuberosum.

